course: dictionary
lesson: 7523
title: One word, many meanings: practice
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and practice is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence? «Skills grow with practice: ten minutes every day builds a skill much faster than one long session a week.» Here practice means doing something again and again to get better.
explain: «Rory missed football practice as a punishment, and kept looking at Finn.» Here practice is not an activity you repeat. Football practice is a training session where a team meets. The words football and missed are your clues.
explain: «It is good practice to wash your hands before you eat.» Here practice means the usual way of doing something, a habit. Always test your meaning by putting it back into the sentence, and check that it still makes sense.
explain: In UK English, the noun is practice and the verb is practise, with an s. You practise the piano, and you have piano practice. In US English, practice is used for both the noun and the verb.
fact: Practice (noun) means doing something again and again to get better at it.
fact: A practice can be a team's training session, or the place where a doctor or dentist works.
fact: «Practice makes perfect» means that the more you do something, the better you become at it.
fact: In UK English the verb is spelt practise; in US English practice is used for both the verb and the noun.
fact: Practice only helps if it is accurate, so check your work carefully, not just how often you do it.
exercise: «Skills grow with practice: ten minutes every day builds a skill much faster than one long session a week.» What does practice mean in this sentence? | A warning sign that something hurts | The place where a doctor works | *Doing something again and again to get better | A team's training meeting
exercise: «Rory missed football practice as a punishment, and kept looking at Finn.» What is football practice? | *A training session where a team meets | A doctor's visit for an injury | A habit that a player has every day | A long walk around the pitch
exercise: In UK English, which spelling is the verb? Lucy will ___ the violin every day. | *practise | practiced | practice | practyse
test: «It is good practice to wash your hands before you eat.» What does practice mean here? | A doctor's office | A kind of hand cream | *The usual way something is done, a habit | A team training session
test: Dr Shah works at the surgery on the high street, so she sees patients there every day. What is a practice? | A warning that something is wrong | Doing a sum again and again | *The place where a doctor or dentist works | Training for a sport
exam: Asha practises the piano for 12 minutes every day. How many minutes does she practise in 5 days? | 120 | 17 | *60 | 7
